    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test \u2014 the only concrete test class is `AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `checkDigit` is a derived, read-only owner field \u2014 the same shape as existing derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `identityKey`, `locality`), so I followed that convention exactly to keep structural impact minimal.\n\n1. **New file** `CheckDigit.java` \u2014 a small, cohesive `final` class with one static `of(Owner)` that computes the Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode` (mirrors `MembershipLevel`/`IdentityKey`). New class \u2192 zero surrounding complexity to hold.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"...CheckDigit.of(owner)\")` line to `toOwnerDto`. That method's CC is 1 and I changed a single line, so the cost here is tiny.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` schema property (int, 0\u20139, readOnly) so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n\nNo existing method grew and no large class was edited: the actual logic lives in a fresh single-method class, and the two edits to existing files are one line each.\n\nThe endpoint serves it automatically \u2014 `RespondWithOwner` maps the entity through `toOwnerDto`, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `checkDigit`, which the acceptance test verifies against its own Luhn recomputation.",
